                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Absolutely not !\nAbysmal level design.\n\nFor instance, you drop down a pit without a clue of what's coming, spot a passage in a wall that requires previous knowledge to be accessed, land on an floor visited earlier (all mobs respawned,) and now need to re-traverse 20 screens to get back up to the pit with the passage (all mobs respawned along the way.)\nSod off, game !\n\nYet worse are all the (mandatory) spots that you cannot climb to once you killed the mobs: You must use combat jumps to reach those platforms.\nSod off, game !\n\nNo wonder they respawn on every screen transition.\nIt's not like combat is worth repeating; in fact it's not good enough to justify fighting at all.\nAnd the traversal isn't very good either, what with ladders that refuse to get grabbed, imprecise jumps, etc.\nShould have expected the direness as soon as I was introduced to the idiotic, irritating, counter-standard menu controls.",
